# Installation

## 1. Clone the Repository

Clone the project from the repository:

```bash
git clone https://git.code.sf.net/p/atifgr/code atifgr
```

Enter the project directory:

```bash
cd atifgr
```

> If the repository clone URL shown on the SourceForge **Code** page differs, use the current URL provided there.

---

## 2. Install Dependencies

Run:

```bash
npm install
```

This installs the dependencies required by the application.

---

## 3. Configure Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root if required by the current application configuration.

Example:

```env
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
```

If AI functionality is enabled, configure the required Gemini API credential:

```env
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
```

Do not commit API keys, passwords, or other sensitive credentials to GitHub.

---

## 4. Start the Development Server

Run:

```bash
npm run dev
```

The application will normally be available at:

```text
http://localhost:3000
```

The actual port may vary depending on the project configuration.

---

# Production Build

Before deploying the application to a production server, create the production build:

```bash
npm run build
```

After a successful build, the compiled application can be started using the production server.

