# Running with PM2

PM2 is used to keep the Node.js application running continuously and restart it when necessary.

## 1. Install PM2

```bash
npm install -g pm2
```

---

## 2. Start ATIF HIS

Run:

```bash
NODE_ENV=production pm2 start dist/server.cjs --name atif
```

Check the application:

```bash
pm2 status
```

The application should show:

```text
atif    online
```

---

## 3. View Logs

```bash
pm2 logs atif
```

---

## 4. Restart the Application

```bash
pm2 restart atif
```

---

## 5. Stop the Application

```bash
pm2 stop atif
```

---

## 6. Save the PM2 Process

```bash
pm2 save
```

---

## 7. Enable Automatic Startup

Run:

```bash
pm2 startup
```

PM2 will display a command that should be executed to configure automatic startup.

After executing the generated command:

```bash
pm2 save
```

ATIF HIS will then automatically restart after a server reboot.

