# Nginx Configuration

Nginx can be used as a reverse proxy between the public domain and the Node.js application.

## 1. Install Nginx

```bash
sudo apt install nginx -y
```

Check the service:

```bash
sudo systemctl status nginx
```

---

## 2. Create the ATIF Configuration

Create a new configuration file:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/atif
```

Add:

```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;

    server_name YOUR_DOMAIN;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;

        proxy_http_version 1.1;

        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
    }
}
```

Replace:

```text
YOUR_DOMAIN
```

with your actual domain.

---

## 3. Enable the Configuration

```bash
sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/atif /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/atif
```

If the default Nginx configuration is enabled, remove it:

```bash
sudo rm /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default
```

---

## 4. Test Nginx

Always test the configuration:

```bash
sudo nginx -t
```

If the test is successful:

```bash
sudo systemctl reload nginx
```

---

# SSL / HTTPS Configuration

HTTPS is recommended for production deployments.

Install Certbot:

```bash
sudo apt install certbot python3-certbot-nginx -y
```

Request an SSL certificate:

```bash
sudo certbot --nginx -d YOUR_DOMAIN
```

Follow the instructions provided by Certbot.

After successful configuration, the application will be available through:

```text
https://YOUR_DOMAIN
```

